# Credentials and API endpoints for Bridged Self-Distillation (BSD).
#
# Copy this file to .env in the repository root and fill it in:
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
# .env is git-ignored. Never commit it and never paste a key into a script.
#
# Three recipe scripts load .env automatically (BSD_DOTENV_PATH selects
# another file):
#   recipes/bsd/scripts/03_generate_closed_teacher_traces.sh
#   recipes/bsd/scripts/04_build_ropd_teacher_index.sh
#   recipes/bsd/scripts/run_ropd_multi.sh
# Every other script and tool reads only the process environment. Export the
# file before running one of them:
#   set -a; source .env; set +a
#
# The file is sourced by bash: plain NAME=value lines, no spaces around "=".
# A value set here replaces a variable of the same name that is already
# exported in the shell. Optional variables are commented out; uncomment only
# the ones you set, because an empty value is not the same as an unset variable.

# --- Closed-API external teacher ---------------------------------------------
# Base URL, key and model id of an OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint.
# All three are required by tools/bsd/generate_closed_teacher_data.py,
# which 03_generate_closed_teacher_traces.sh runs to generate the teacher traces.
CLOSED_TEACHER_BASE_URL=
CLOSED_TEACHER_API_KEY=
CLOSED_TEACHER_MODEL=
# Reasoning effort that 03_generate_closed_teacher_traces.sh passes to the endpoint
# (default: medium).
# CLOSED_TEACHER_REASONING_EFFORT=medium

# --- ROPD baseline: teacher answers, rubricator and verifier -----------------
# Read by 04_build_ropd_teacher_index.sh and run_ropd_multi.sh. The
# key and the base URL default to CLOSED_TEACHER_API_KEY and
# CLOSED_TEACHER_BASE_URL, the three model ids to CLOSED_TEACHER_MODEL. Set
# them only when ROPD should use another endpoint or another model.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=your-api-key
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.example.invalid/v1
# ROPD_TEACHER_MODEL=provider-model-id
# ROPD_RUBRICATOR_MODEL=provider-model-id
# ROPD_VERIFIER_MODEL=provider-model-id
# The provider profiles and the remaining ROPD_* settings are in
# recipes/bsd/configs/ropd_judge_providers.yaml.

# --- OpenRouter --------------------------------------------------------------
# Required by tools/bsd/generate_pi_forms.py, which generates the hints
# and the guides of BSD-hint and BSD-guide. It is also the key of the
# "openrouter" profile in ropd_judge_providers.yaml.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your-openrouter-api-key

# --- Weights & Biases (optional) ---------------------------------------------
# By default training logs to the console only. BSD_ENABLE_WANDB=1 adds the
# W&B logger, and the wandb client then reads the key below. Of the training
# launchers only run_ropd_multi.sh loads .env: export these variables
# in the shell for the others.
# BSD_ENABLE_WANDB=1
# WANDB_API_KEY=your-wandb-api-key
# WANDB_ENTITY=your-wandb-entity
